D-001, an oral small molecule inhibitor of receptor-interacting protein kinase 2, which is in phase 2a trial for the treatment of ulcerative colitis; OD-002, an oral small molecule SLC15A4 inhibitor designed to block TLR7/8/9-mediated pathogenic inflammatory responses activation of interferon regulatory factor 5 (IRF5); OD-003, a protein therapeutic designed to agonize tumor necrosis factor receptor 2 selectively on Treg; a TSLP/IL-33 bispecific antagonist; an oral small molecule interleukin-1 receptor\u0096associated kinase 4 scaffolding inhibitor; and a small molecule inhibitor of IRF5. The company was incorporated in 2021 and is headquartered in Boston, Massachusetts.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Gary D. Glick Ph.D. | Founder, President, CEO & Director | Age 63 | Compensation: $558,900 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 100 people. Revenue per employee of $30K ranks in the bottom quartile among Healthcare peers. Stock-based compensation of $143K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 19\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). R&D investment of 4255% of revenue (heavy) signals commitment to product development and talent. Note: heavy R&D investment has not yet translated to above-average workforce productivity \u2014 watch for commercialisation lag.","financial_summary":["Odyssey Therapeutics, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $920M market cap on $3M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +69% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","The company is burning through $131M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -9479.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 23.1% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and stock-based comp at 481% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 6.2% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-3.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"SGA costs surged 38% YoY \u2014 may reflect legal, restructuring, or operational issues","sev":"red","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Operating margins 5415% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.0% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 126% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Large open-market insider purchases (net $55.1M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","Growing faster than most Healthcare peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","R&D investment (4255% of revenue) is above Healthcare peers, supporting innovation","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term averag